                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8ceb7d9d-4112-35b9-85fe-dd060ebc3fd5",
                        "entry_id": "ae726fc6-d57b-3412-9fb8-bf60dca9df7d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To belch, to burp."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Geordie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "63f33073-886f-4bef-ae22-5a8f09ca72f3",
                                "sense_id": "8ceb7d9d-4112-35b9-85fe-dd060ebc3fd5",
                                "text": "\"That made me bowk,\" he said; and he bowked again. He took another swig with caution, and gave the bottle to David, and they swigged at it in turn."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b257afa2-0c25-4e23-b46b-6f50ec018cbf",
                                "sense_id": "8ceb7d9d-4112-35b9-85fe-dd060ebc3fd5",
                                "text": "If this man did not feed the mill carefully and regularly it bowked with \"indigestion\" and this slowed everything up."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db25532f-aad7-4ba0-8bd6-6786a5d12cf8",
                                "sense_id": "8ceb7d9d-4112-35b9-85fe-dd060ebc3fd5",
                                "text": "He claimed that meat or cheese made you 'bowk' (belch) and get stomach cramps — the last thing you need 'yakking' (using a pick) coal for eight tough hours in a two-foot 'cavil' (job area)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b1949a1f-db8f-3762-8cb2-f8b08e2a00ac",
                        "entry_id": "ae726fc6-d57b-3412-9fb8-bf60dca9df7d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To vomit."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "debb4559-5fdf-4bb5-a938-ac3bfa6c3ae0",
                                "sense_id": "b1949a1f-db8f-3762-8cb2-f8b08e2a00ac",
                                "text": "At that point another of my guests, a highly respected Newcastle art gallery owner by the name of Rashida, bowked up all over the floor behind me."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "95ece4c3-5896-411c-9206-e54a6d849249",
                                "sense_id": "b1949a1f-db8f-3762-8cb2-f8b08e2a00ac",
                                "text": "'Take yourself to bed then. And don't whine to me tomorrow about how you bowked your guts out all night.'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e645eb76-edf3-4acb-aa14-dfd347cda323",
                                "sense_id": "b1949a1f-db8f-3762-8cb2-f8b08e2a00ac",
                                "text": "Firstly, aged perhaps five or six after polishing off a banana and a slice of bread and butter in the back room at tea time, taking my plate out to the kitchen, I managed to make it only as far as the spin dryer in the hall before bowking richly over the lino."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "565d3169-ad6c-4643-82d2-09e76381cf8d",
                                "sense_id": "b1949a1f-db8f-3762-8cb2-f8b08e2a00ac",
                                "text": "Misima bowked beside him, bent over double. They made twin streams of yellow bile in the heather."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
